rom":5},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":30,"verseEnd":30,"votes":15,"source":"openbible","text":"After forty years had passed, an angel appeared to Moses in the flames of a burning bush in the desert near Mount Sinai.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":35,"verseEnd":35,"votes":15,"source":"openbible","text":"This Moses, whom they had rejected with the words, ‘Who made you ruler and judge?’ is the one whom God sent to be their ruler and redeemer through the angel who appeared to him in the bush.","from":2},{"book":"EXO","chapter":19,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"And you are to set up a boundary for the people around the mountain and tell them, ‘Be careful not to go up on the mountain or touch its base. Whoever touches the mountain shall surely be put to death.","from":5},{"book":"ISA","chapter":43,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"When you pass through the waters, I will be with you; and when you go through the rivers, they will not overwhelm you. When you walk through the fire, you will not be scorched; the flames will not set you ablaze.","from":2},{"book":"ACT","chapter":7,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":12,"source":"both","text":"Then the Lord said to him, ‘Take off your sandals, for the place where you are standing is holy ground.","from":5},{"book":"LUK","chapter":20,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Even Moses demonstrates that the dead are raised, in the passage about the burning bush. For he calls the Lord ‘the God of Abraham, the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob.’","from":6},{"book":"DEU","chapter":33,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"with the choice gifts of the land and everything in it, and with the favor of Him who dwelt in the burning bush. May these rest on the head of Joseph and crown the brow of the prince of his brothers.","from":2}],"notes":[{"id":"moses-greater","title":"Moses and Christ, servant and Son","kind":"type"}],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3},{"id":"exodus-family","title":"Moses and his circle","people":2}]},"7-12":{"people":[{"id":"amorites-h0567","name":"Amorites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"heth-h2845","name":"Heth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Canaan","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"hivites-h2340","name":"Hivites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"jebusites-h2983g","name":"Jebusites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanite tribe","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"perizzites-h6522","name":"Perizzites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":9},{"id":"pharaoh-h6547j","name":"Pharaoh","kind":"person","brief":"A Pharaoh","count":2,"firstVerse":10},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":6,"firstVerse":7},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8}],"words":[{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":641},{"base":"H6818","lemma":"צְעָקָה","tr":"tsa·a·qah","gloss":"cry","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":21},{"base":"H3318","lemma":"יָצָא","tr":"ya·tsa","gloss":"to come out: come","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1067},{"base":"H6547","lemma":"פַּרְעֹה","tr":"par·oh","gloss":"Pharaoh","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":274},{"base":"H0595","lemma":"אָֽנֹכִ֫י","tr":"a·no·khi","gloss":"I","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":359},{"base":"H6258","lemma":"עַתָּ֫ה","tr":"at·tah","gloss":"now","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":433},{"base":"H7971","lemma":"שָׁלַח","tr":"sha·lach","gloss":"to send: depart","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":847},{"base":"H3906","lemma":"לַ֫חַץ","tr":"la·chats","gloss":"oppression","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H4341","lemma":"מַכְאוֹב","tr":"makh·ov","gloss":"pain","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H3905","lemma":"לָחַץ","tr":"la·chats","gloss":"to oppress","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":19}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":145,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":25,"source":"both","text":"He fulfills the desires of those who fear Him; He hears their cry and saves them.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":106,"verse":44,"verseEnd":44,"votes":23,"source":"both","text":"Nevertheless He heard their cry; He took note of their distress.","from":7},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"After a long time, the king of Egypt died. The Israelites groaned and cried out under their burden of slavery, and their cry for deliverance from bondage ascended to God.","from":7},{"book":"EXO","chapter":2,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":19,"source":"openbible","text":"God saw the Israelites and took notice.","from":7},{"book":"JOS","chapter":1,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":19,"source":"both","text":"No one shall stand against you all the days of your life. As I was with Moses, so will I be with you; I will never leave you nor forsake you.","from":12},{"book":"GEN","chapter":50,"verse":24,"verseEnd":24,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"Then Joseph said to his brothers, “I am about to die, but God will surely visit you and bring you up from this land to the land He promised on oath to Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob.”","from":8},{"book":"ROM","chapter":8,"verse":31,"verseEnd":31,"votes":18,"source":"both","text":"What then shall we say in response to these things? If God is for us, who can be against us?","from":12},{"book":"EXO","chapter":3,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"And I have promised to bring you up out of your affliction in Egypt, into the land of the Canaanites, Hittites, Amorites, Perizzites, Hivites, and Jebusites—a land flowing with milk and honey.’","from":8}],"notes":[{"id":"moses-greater","title":"Moses and Christ, servant and Son","kind":"type"}],"groups":[]},"13-15":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":3,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"moses-h4872","name":"Moses","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Amram","count":3,"firstVerse":13},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":15},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":15}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H4872","lemma":"מֹשֶׁה","tr":"mo·sheh","gloss":"Moses","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":766},{"base":"H7971","lemma":"שָׁלַח","tr":"sha·lach","gloss":"to send: depart","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":847},{"base":"H1755","lemma":"דּוֹר","tr":"dor","gloss":"generation","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":167},{"base":"H3541","lemma":"כֹּה","tr":"koh","gloss":"thus","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":577},{"base":"H4100","lemma":"מָה","tr":"mah","gloss":"what?","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":752},{"base":"H8034","lemma":"שֵׁם","tr":"shem","gloss":"name","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":864},{"base":"H2143","lemma":"זֵ֫כֶר","tr":"ze·kher","gloss":"memorial","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H2088","lemma":"זֶה","tr":"zeh","gloss":"this","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1176},{"base":"H3327","lemma":"יִצְחָק","tr":"yits·chaq","gloss":"Isaac","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":108},{"base":"H0085","lemma":"אַבְרָהָם","tr":"av·ra·ham","gloss":"Abraham","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":175}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"HEB","chapter":13,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":52,"source":"both","text":"Jesus Christ is the same yesterday and today and forever.","from":14},{"book":"JHN","chapter":8,"verse":58,"verseEnd":58,"votes":51,"source":"both","text":"“Truly, truly, I tell you,” Jesus declared, “before Abraham was born, I am!”","from":14},{"book":"REV","chapter":1,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":42,"source":"both","text":"“I am the Alpha and the Omega,” says the Lord God, who is and was and is to come—the Almighty.","from":14},{"book":"PSA","chapter":90,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":38,"source":"both","text":"Before the mountains were born or You brought forth the earth and the world, from everlasting to everlasting You are God.","from":14},{"book":"ISA","chapter":44,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":32,"source":"both","text":"Thus says the LORD, the King and Redeemer of Israel, the LORD of Hosts: “I am the first and I am the last, and there is no God but Me.","from":14},{"book":"REV","chapter":1,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":24,"source":"both","text":"John, To the seven churches in the province of Asia: Grace and peace to you from Him who is and was and is to come, and from the seven spirits before His throne,","from":14},{"book":"EXO","chapter":6,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"I appeared to Abraham, to Isaac, and to Jacob as God Almighty, but by My name the LORD I did not make Myself known to them.","from":14},{"book":"REV","chapter":1,"verse":17,"verseEnd":17,"votes":22,"source":"both","text":"When I saw Him, I fell at His feet like a dead man. But He placed His right hand on me and said, “Do not be afraid. I am the First and the Last,","from":14}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"16-22":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"abraham-h0085","name":"Abraham","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Terah","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"isaac-h3327","name":"Isaac","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"amorites-h0567","name":"Amorites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"heth-h2845","name":"Heth","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Canaan","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"hivites-h2340","name":"Hivites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"jebusites-h2983g","name":"Jebusites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanite tribe","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"perizzites-h6522","name":"Perizzites","kind":"person","brief":"Canaanites","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"hebrews-h5680","name":"Hebrews","kind":"person","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":18}],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":7,"firstVerse":16},{"id":"canaan-h3667a","name":"Canaan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":17}],"words":[{"base":"H4713","lemma":"מִצְרִי","tr":"mits·ri","gloss":"Egyptian","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":70},{"base":"H4714","lemma":"מִצְרַ֫יִם","tr":"mits·ra·yim","gloss":"Egypt","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":641},{"base":"H2205","lemma":"זָקֵן","tr":"za·qen","gloss":"old: elder","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":178},{"base":"H6485","lemma":"פָּקַד","tr":"pa·qad","gloss":"to reckon: list","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":303},{"base":"H3627","lemma":"כְּלִי","tr":"ke·li","gloss":"article","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":325},{"base":"H7971","lemma":"שָׁלַח","tr":"sha·lach","gloss":"to send: depart","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":847},{"base":"H7387","lemma":"רֵיקָם","tr":"re·qam","gloss":"emptily","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":16},{"base":"H7934","lemma":"שָׁכֵן","tr":"sha·khen","gloss":"neighboring","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H6522","lemma":"פְּרִזִּי","tr":"pe·riz·zi","gloss":"Perizzite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":23},{"base":"H2340","lemma":"חִוִּי","tr":"chiv·vi","gloss":"Hivite","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":25}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EXO","chapter":12,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":17,"source":"both","text":"And the LORD gave the people such favor in the sight of the Egyptians that they granted their request. In this way they plundered the Egyptians.","from":21},{"book":"PSA","chapter":105,"verse":37,"verseEnd":37,"votes":12,"source":"openbible","text":"He brought Israel out with silver and gold, and none among His tribes stumbled.","from":21},{"book":"EXO","chapter":9,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Then the LORD said to Moses, “Go to Pharaoh and tell him that this is what the LORD, the God of the Hebrews, says: ‘Let My people go, so that they may worship Me.","from":18},{"book":"EXO","chapter":11,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"And the LORD gave the people favor in the sight of the Egyptians. Moreover, Moses himself was highly regarded in Egypt by Pharaohʼs officials and by the people.","from":21},{"book":"PRO","chapter":16,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":10,"source":"both","text":"When a manʼs ways please the LORD, He makes even the manʼs enemies live at peace with him.","from":21},{"book":"EXO","chapter":7,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"Then say to him, ‘The LORD, the God of the Hebrews, has sent me to tell you: Let My people go, so that they may worship Me in the wilderness. But until now you have not listened.","from":18},{"book":"PSA","chapter":106,"verse":46,"verseEnd":46,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"He made them objects of compassion to all who held them captive.","from":21},{"book":"GEN","chapter":39,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"the Lordwas with him and extended kindness to him, granting him favor in the eyes of the prison warden.","from":21}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]}}